            <div xml:id="d902">

                <pb facs="0810" n="798" sameAs="frus:frus1942v04/pg798"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.248/590: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Ambassador in Turkey</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Steinhardt</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1942-06-23T15:00:00-04:00">June 23, 1942—3
                            p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>294. Your 653, June 22, 1 p.m. and 655, June 22. The following telegram has been
                    sent to Cairo.</p>
                <quote rend="blockquote">
                    <p>“Your June 14, 5 p.m. to Ankara. General Arnold is instructing Colonel
                        Halverson that disposition of planes and personnel in Turkey is now a
                        subject of diplomatic negotiations being conducted by the State Department
                        and that no military official should proceed to Turkey in connection with
                        the matter.</p>
                    <p>Repeated to Ankara.”</p>
                </quote>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Hull</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
